0,Napu language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_639:npy,"July 10, 2025 - Napu is an Austronesian language spoken in the North Lore district of Central Sulawesi, Indonesia.",Napu,Austronesian
1,Austronesian peoples - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austronesian_peoples,1 week ago - Gong ensembles are also a common musical heritage of Island Southeast Asia. The casting of gong instruments is believed to have originated from the Bronze Age cultures of Mainland Southeast Asia. It spread to the Austronesian islands initially through trade as prestige goods.,Napu,Austronesian
2,Taiwanese Indigenous pop music - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiwanese_Indigenous_pop_music,"March 26, 2026 - Taiwanese Indigenous pop music comprises contemporary songs performed in Austronesian languages native to Taiwan, blending modern pop music with Indigenous linguistic and cultural elements. It has steadily gained mainstream recognition over the past two decades, reflecting a broader cultural ...",Napu,Austronesian
3,Napu in Indonesia people group profile | Joshua Project,https://www.joshuaproject.net/people_groups/13952/ID,"Celebrations often include traditional dances, music, and feasts during harvest seasons or weddings. Meals are based on rice, vegetables, and occasionally meat, reflecting the agricultural lifestyle of the region. ... The Napu people have been influenced by Christianity, particularly Protestant traditions introduced through missionary work.",Napu,Austronesian
